Z||000005||Old Lar||12-07-2001||08:12 AM||||I am thinking that the Darwin theory will come into play for those who want their Fieros just for more speed.<P>There is a rev limiter on the V6 Fieros that kick in around 6000 rpm.  In the stock form there just aren't enough horses in the engine to get up to 6000 rpms in 4th gear.<P>140 kph = 87 mph doable in a stock Fiero.<BR>200 kph = 123 mph doable in a stock 2.8 V6.<P>Just how fast is fast enough on the street?<P><BR>||||reg||1
Z||000006||jelly2m8||12-07-2001||10:10 AM||||Look at my sig.<P> Stock canadian vesion of the 120mph speedo.<BR>Stock 2.8L 5 spd Getrag, 66k kilometers.<P>Needle will sit on the pin which is about 200kph at ~4800 rpm. I've had this car up to 5700 rpm in 5th, how fast will they go? dunno, but fast enough to stay with most cars on the road.<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://users.eastlink.ca/~acook1/pegged%2001.jpg"> ||||reg||1
