Z||000009||Zoom88||12-07-2001||01:44 PM|||| Well lets see, I have a 88 Formula I have opened up the exhaust manifolds, installed an Ocelot exhaust system, timing is at 12 deg<BR>and other than that it is stock. I have a neighbor that has access to radar equip. living out in the rural country we setup and he clocked me at 129 mph, I stayed in 4th gear, don't know what the exact RPM was but I know It wasn't redlining. Motor has 120,000 miles on it. Only problem I have with the motor is that it surges or hunts up and down while idling I have just about tried everything I can think of or read on this forum to resolve the problem seems to no avail. I would like to try another ECM since the Guy I bought it from says it has done it since day one, he even had it in and out the shop till he finally gave up on it.<BR> Guess I Need to go to the mall and try to locate a ECM for an 88 v6 5 speed.||||reg||1
Z||000010||Howard_Sacks||12-07-2001||03:05 PM||||These are old cars.  I wouldn't drive that fast for an extended period of time in them.  I know from experience. I drove from exit 4 of the NJ turnpike (philly) to the George Washington bridge (new york) in under 45 min and my 86 was not the same afterwords. (Everyone is going to ask but, oil was synth with only 1000miles on it changed 5 weeks prior to land speed record :-))<P>btw, I'm not too crazy, the roads were clear and it was 3AM.||||reg||1
